<p>
    Consider the alternating geometric series
    <me>
        S = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} (-1)^k \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^k = 1 - \frac{4}{5} + \frac{16}{25} - \cdots + (-1)^{n-1} \left( \frac{4}{5} \right)^{n-1} + \cdots
    </me>
    We want to explore how the partial sums of the series compare to and approximate the exact sum of the series.
</p>
<!-- This activity needs every bit of extra width it can get in PreTeXt, so I'm not using <ol>. -->
  <p>
      a. Recall that the <m>n</m>th partial sum, <m>S_n</m>, is the sum of the first <m>n</m> terms of the infinite geometric series <m>S</m>.  This means that (use <alert>decimals</alert>, not fractions or expressions):</p>
    <p>
      <m>S_1=a_0=1</m>
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer name="S2" symbolicEquality><label><m>S_2=a_0+a_1=1-\frac{4}{5}=</m></label>0.2</answer>
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer name="S3" symbolicEquality><label><m>S_3=a_0+a_1+a_2=1-\frac{4}{5}+\frac{16}{25}=</m></label>0.84</answer>
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer name="S4" symbolicEquality><label><m>S_4=S_3+\left(-\frac{64}{125}\right)=</m></label>0.328</answer>
    </p>
    <p>
      <m>S_5=S_4+\left(\frac{4}{5}\right)^4=0.7376</m>
    </p>
    <p>
      <m>S_6=S_5+a_5=0.40992</m>
    </p>
    <p>
      Recall also that the exact sum of the infinite series is
            <me>S = \frac{a}{1-r} = \frac{1}{1-\left(\frac{-4}{5}\right)} = \frac{1}{\frac{9}{5}} = \frac{5}{9}</me>
    </p>
    <p>
      Your task is to use this information to do some related computations that help us understand the behavior of the series and its partial sums.
            </p>
            <p>
                First, compute the differences between <m>S_n</m> and <m>S</m> for several different values of <m>n</m>, and fill in the first column of blank spaces provided below with <alert>decimal</alert> answers.  In addition, fill in <alert>decimal</alert> representations of <m>a_3</m>, <m>\ldots</m>, <m>a_6</m> to compare to the differences in the adjacent column. If the decimal terminates, use all digits.  For any nonterminating decimal representations, be accurate to within at least <m>0.00001</m>.
            </p>
<div sectionWideCheckWork forceIndividualAnswerColoring>
       <p>
         <m>n = 1 \hspace{.25in} S_1 = 1 \hspace{.7in} S_1 - S = </m><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number displayDecimals="6">4/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_1 = -0.8</m>
       </p>
      <p>
         <m>n = 2 \hspace{.25in} S_2 = </m><mathInput disabled minWidth="20"><conditionalContent condition="$S2.creditAchieved=1">$S2</conditionalContent></mathInput><m> \hspace{.5in} S_2 - S = </m><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number displayDecimals="6">0.2-5/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_2 = 0.64</m>
       </p>
      <p>
         <m>n = 3 \hspace{.25in} S_3= </m><mathInput disabled minWidth="30"><conditionalContent condition="$S3.creditAchieved=1">$S3</conditionalContent></mathInput><m>\hspace{.4in} S_3 - S = </m><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number displayDecimals="6">0.84-5/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_3 =</m><answer>-0.512</answer>
       </p>
    <p>
         <m>n = 4 \hspace{.25in} S_4= </m><mathInput disabled minWidth="40"><conditionalContent condition="$S4.creditAchieved=1">$S4</conditionalContent></mathInput><m>\hspace{.35in} S_4 - S = </m><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number displayDecimals="6">0.328-5/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_4 =</m><answer>0.4096</answer>
       </p>
    <p>
         <m>n = 5 \hspace{.25in} S_5= 0.7376 \hspace{.3in} S_5 - S = </m><answer symbolicEquality allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute><number displayDecimals="6">0.7376-5/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_5 =</m><answer>-0.32768</answer>
       </p>
  <p>
         <m>n = 6 \hspace{.25in} S_6= 0.40992 \hspace{.25in} S_6 - S = </m><answer allowedErrorInNumbers="0.00001" allowedErrorIsAbsolute symbolicEquality><number displayDecimals="6">0.40992-5/9</number></answer><m> \hspace{.3in} a_6 =</m><answer>0.262144</answer>
       </p>

</div>
            <p>
                b. What do you notice about the differences between <m>S_n</m> and <m>S</m> as the value of <m>n</m> increases?  Check all of the following statements that are true.
            </p>
      <p>
        <answer selectMultiple>
          <choiceInput>
            <choice><m>S_n - S</m> always decreases in value as <m>n</m> increases</choice>
            <choice credit="1"><m>S_n - S</m> alternates in sign as <m>n</m> increases</choice>
            <choice credit="1">The value of the partial sum, <m>S_n</m>, is always getting closer to <m>S</m> as <m>n</m> increases</choice>
            <choice><m>S_n - S</m> is always positive</choice>
            <choice credit="1"><m>|S_n - S|</m> always decreases in value as <m>n</m> increases</choice>
          </choiceInput>
        </answer>
      </p>
            <p>
               c. What do you notice about how the differences between <m>S_n</m> and <m>S</m> compare to the value of <m>a_n</m>? There are at least two important things you can say.
            </p>
      <p>
        <answer selectMultiple>
          <choiceInput>
            <choice><m>S_n - S \lt a_n</m> for each value of <m>n</m> </choice>
            <choice><m>S_n - S</m> has the same sign as <m>a_n</m></choice>
            <choice credit="1"><m>S_n - S</m> has the opposite sign as <m>a_n</m></choice>
            <choice credit="1"><m>|S_n - S| \lt |a_n|</m> for each value of <m>n</m> </choice>
            <choice credit="1">The absolute difference between <m>S_n</m> and <m>S</m> is always less than the absolute value of the next term in the sum</choice>
          </choiceInput>
        </answer>
      </p>